# Host-card open (chat command)

When the user says `open …` / `reopen …` with a project name (and CODE when required), **run the CLI immediately**. This is **not** MCP `olie-flow-ai`, not a board lookup, and not “explain the card”. Do **not** ask what the CODE means, which workspace to use, or which tool to wait for. CWD does not matter — use the absolute path below. Normalize CODE to uppercase (`dop-1183` → `DOP-1183`).

## With CODE (funnel cards)

Projects: `olie`, `locav`, `televisao` (and any other that uses `{{ code }}` / DOP-… / LCV-…).

User: `open olie DOP-1183` / `open olie dop-1183` / `reopen locav LCV-17` →

```bash
~/git/bin/workvm-host-card open --project <PROJECT> --code <CODE>
```

Print `workspace=` and `api_worktree=` from the CLI output. Then stop unless the user asks for more.

## Without CODE (funnel only)

User: `open olie` / `open locav` / `reopen televisao` **with no card code**:

- Stop and ask for the code (ex.: `DOP-1258`).
- Optional: `~/git/bin/workvm-host-card list` as reference only.
- Never guess (last card, only on list, “most recent”).

## Single-unit (no DOP)

`use-url-query`, `opbed`, `boilerplate-laravel`, `boilerplate-next`, `fabriciogferreira`.

User: `open use-url-query` / `open opbed` (no second token) →

```bash
~/git/bin/workvm-host-card open --project <PROJECT> --code <PROJECT>
```

Do not ask for CODE. If the CLI does not list the project yet, say so and stop — do not invent CODE.
